// Generated by scripts/build-icon-kits.py from the Gallery and Pocket Tech
// icon kits. Regenerate it rather than editing it.
//
// The pictograms are in curveKits.ts: all four curved kits draw the same
// subjects, and the generator refuses to emit anything if that stops being
// true. This file is only what sits behind them.
//
// Gallery is a glossy paint drop on warm paper, and the pigment is assigned per
// icon from a four-colour palette rather than per cluster — a rotation, so a
// screen of them reads as a painter's shelf rather than a legend. Pocket Tech
// is smoked glass and satin silver, one material for every icon, and its
// hierarchy is carried by the shape of the casing instead: a rounded shell for
// a cluster, a round jewel for a hobby.

// Gallery: one carrier for everything, and the pigment is the only variable.
//
// Clusters and hobbies are drawn the same way here, which is the kit's own
// decision and worth knowing: in this set the drawing does not say which is
// which, so the layout around it has to. Everywhere the app uses a mark today
// that is already true — Discover and Collection label every entry.
